  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (175 tests, 0 failed, including the 10 new ones).\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):** all six store rules are implemented as specified, with `store.clock()` as the only time source. I added `getAvailable`, `reserve`, `confirm` and `release`, and `removeItem` now checks against available stock instead of physical stock.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** the four endpoint changes return the statuses you listed. `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`.\n- **Tests:** new cases in `test/store.test.js` and `test/api.test.js` use an injected clock to cover the expiry boundary, one-shot confirm, idempotent release, reserved stock blocking `removeItem`, and each API status code.\n\nBehaviours the spec didn't cover:\n- `reserve` doesn't validate `ttlMs`.\n- A `POST /reservations` error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400 with the error message.\n- Confirming an expired reservation deletes it, so a second confirm returns `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`. Unconfirmed expired reservations stay in memory.",
